+<!doctype html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+  <meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
+  <meta name="theme-color" content="#0c252e">
+  <meta name="description" content="An underwater expedition notebook for learning how a Kalman filter predicts, corrects, and sometimes gets it wrong.">
+  <title>Abyss — a Kalman field notebook</title>
+  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
+  <script defer src="filter.js"></script><script defer src="app.js"></script>
+</head>
+<body>
+  <a class="skip" href="#mission">Skip to mission controls</a>
+  <header class="masthead">
+    <a href="../secret/" class="home-link">← Secret projects</a>
+    <a href="#" class="wordmark" aria-label="Abyss home">abyss<span> / FIELD NOTES</span></a>
+    <span class="edition">ROBOTICS LAB <b>№ 04</b></span>
+  </header>
+  <main>
+    <section class="introduction" aria-labelledby="title">
+      <div><p class="eyebrow">AN EXPEDITION INTO UNCERTAINTY</p><h1 id="title">Find your way.<br><em>Even when you can’t see.</em></h1></div>
+      <div class="intro-copy"><p>A robot’s sensors tell an imperfect story. Help a little sub find its depth by blending what it <strong>expects</strong> with what it <strong>observes</strong>.</p><a href="#notebook">Open the field notebook <span>↘</span></a></div>
+    </section>
+    <noscript><div class="no-js">This lab needs JavaScript to simulate a mission. A Kalman filter first predicts depth and velocity from motion, then corrects that prediction with a noisy localization fix. Its uncertainty describes the model’s belief, not a guarantee of accuracy. The field notebook below explains the equations.</div></noscript>
+    <div class="lab-layout">
+      <section class="mission-panel" id="mission" aria-labelledby="mission-title">
+        <div class="panel-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / OBSERVE</p><h2 id="mission-title">The quiet-water expedition</h2></div><span class="mission-tag">60 s · 1D DEPTH</span></div>
+        <div class="scene" id="scene">
+          <div class="scene-top"><span><i class="status-dot"></i> <span id="scene-status">Awaiting departure</span></span><span id="clock">00.0 / 60.0 s</span></div>
+          <svg id="ocean" viewBox="0 0 850 340" role="img" aria-labelledby="plot-title plot-description">
+            <title id="plot-title">Underwater depth profile</title>
+            <desc id="plot-description">Time runs left to right; positive depth increases downward. Solid white is truth, orange crosses are localization fixes, mint circles are the estimate, and the shaded mint band is modeled depth uncertainty. Numerical values follow the plot.</desc>
+            <defs>
+              <linearGradient id="water" x2="0" y2="1"><stop stop-color="#174551"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#091e29"/></linearGradient>
+              <pattern id="water-grid" width="52" height="38" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M 52 0 H 0 V 38" fill="none" stroke="#8ac3c4" stroke-opacity=".08"/></pattern>
+              <clipPath id="plot-clip"><rect x="60" y="50" width="740" height="244"/></clipPath>
+            </defs>
+            <rect width="850" height="340" fill="url(#water)"/><rect width="850" height="340" fill="url(#water-grid)"/>
+            <path d="M0 305 Q70 285 132 310 T280 315 T470 307 T640 313 T850 295 V340 H0Z" fill="#16383e"/>
+            <g fill="none" stroke="#447572" stroke-width="2" opacity=".6"><path d="M44 321q-15-30-5-42m5 28 12-17M738 329q-8-35 8-57m-7 34-12-12M764 327q10-18 6-32"/></g>
+            <g id="axes"></g>
+            <g id="checkpoints"></g>
+            <g clip-path="url(#plot-clip)"><path id="band" fill="#9be5c4" fill-opacity=".13"/>
+              <path id="dr-trace" fill="none" stroke="#a7a5cc" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="3 6"/>
+              <path id="comparison-trace" fill="none" stroke="#e9cb7e" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="9 5"/>
+              <path id="truth-trace" fill="none" stroke="#f4f4e6" stroke-width="2"/>
+              <g id="fixes" stroke="#f4a77f" stroke-width="1.8"></g>
+              <path id="estimate-trace" fill="none" stroke="#9be5c4" stroke-width="2.5"/>
+              <g id="estimate-points" fill="#102f38" stroke="#9be5c4" stroke-width="1.5"></g>
+            </g>
+            <g id="sub" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="0" cy="19" rx="26" ry="5" fill="#081b23" opacity=".35"/><path d="M-32-6-42-13v26l10-6" fill="#e5b37e"/><rect x="-31" y="-12" width="59" height="24" rx="12" fill="#efdfb1"/><rect x="-14" y="-18" width="20" height="7" rx="3" fill="#c7ba95"/><circle cx="14" cy="0" r="7" fill="#174551" stroke="#baaa80" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="14" cy="0" r="3" fill="#9be5c4"/><path d="M-21 6h19" stroke="#a99976" stroke-width="2"/></g>
+          </svg>
+          <div class="scene-caption"><span>↓ Depth in meters</span><span>Mission time → <b>Illustrative route, not a map</b></span></div>
+        </div>
+        <div class="legend" aria-label="Plot legend"><span class="truth-key">━ Truth</span><span class="fix-key">× Measured fix</span><span class="estimate-key">○ Estimate + ±2σ band</span><span class="dr-key">┄ Dead reckoning</span></div>
+        <div class="playback"><button id="play" class="primary" disabled>▶ Start mission</button><button id="step" disabled>Step +0.5 s</button><button id="reset" disabled aria-label="Reset and replay this seed">↺ Reset</button><div class="progress"><label for="mission-progress">Mission progress</label><progress id="mission-progress" max="120" value="0"></progress></div></div>
+        <div class="telemetry" aria-label="Current depth telemetry"><div><span>TRUE DEPTH</span><strong id="truth-value">4.00 <small>m</small></strong></div><div><span>MEASURED FIX</span><strong id="fix-value">—</strong></div><div><span>ESTIMATED DEPTH</span><strong id="estimate-value">4.00 <small>m</small></strong></div><div><span>MODELED ±2σ</span><strong id="uncertainty-value">2.00 <small>m</small></strong></div></div>
+        <p id="plot-equivalent" class="plot-equivalent">The mission is paused at 0 seconds. Start or step to receive a fix.</p>
+        <div class="field-tip"><span>FIELD NOTE</span><p id="field-tip">The sub icon marks <strong>ground truth</strong>. The filter never gets to see it. Watch the mint estimate learn from the orange fixes.</p></div>
+        <section class="results" aria-labelledby="results-title"><div class="results-heading"><h3 id="results-title">The mission log</h3><span id="sample-count">0 fixes received</span></div><div class="metrics"><div><span>Raw fix RMSE</span><strong id="raw-rmse">—</strong></div><div><span>Filter RMSE</span><strong id="filter-rmse">—</strong></div><div><span>Dead reckoning RMSE</span><strong id="dr-rmse">—</strong></div></div><p class="small">RMSE is typical depth error; lower is better. Raw fixes use only available samples. Filter and dead reckoning use all elapsed steps.</p><div id="summary" class="summary" hidden></div></section>
+      </section>
+      <aside class="setup" aria-labelledby="setup-title">
+        <p class="eyebrow">YOUR EXPEDITION</p><h2 id="setup-title">Change the conditions.</h2><p class="setup-intro">Same little sub. Four different stories.</p>
+        <fieldset class="scenario"><legend>Choose a mission</legend>
+          <label><input type="radio" name="scenario" value="nominal" checked><span><b>01 &nbsp; Quiet water</b><small>A noisy sensor, a useful model.</small></span></label>
+          <label><input type="radio" name="scenario" value="dropout"><span><b>02 &nbsp; Into the dark</b><small>No fixes from 20–38 seconds.</small></span></label>
+          <label><input type="radio" name="scenario" value="current"><span><b>03 &nbsp; An unseen current</b><small>Motion the model doesn’t know.</small></span></label>
+          <label><input type="radio" name="scenario" value="bias"><span><b>04 &nbsp; A convincing lie</b><small>A +2.5 m bias after 20 seconds.</small></span></label>
+        </fieldset>
+        <div class="control-group"><p class="control-title"><span class="number">A</span> The actual world</p><label for="actual">Sensor noise <span id="actual-label">σ = 1.20 m</span></label><input id="actual" type="range" min="0.2" max="3" step="0.1" value="1.2"><p>Changes the fixes. Random acceleration noise stays at σ = 0.08 m/s².</p></div>
+        <div class="control-group"><p class="control-title"><span class="number">B</span> The filter’s assumptions</p><label for="assumed-r">Measurement noise <span id="r-label">σ = 1.20 m</span></label><input id="assumed-r" type="range" min="0.2" max="4" step="0.1" value="1.2"><label for="assumed-q">Motion disturbance <span id="q-label">σ = 0.08 m/s²</span></label><input id="assumed-q" type="range" min="0.01" max="0.4" step="0.01" value="0.08"><p id="variance-note">R = 1.44 m². Q comes from acceleration variance 0.0064 (m/s²)².</p></div>
+        <div class="seed-control"><label for="seed">Replay seed</label><input id="seed" type="number" min="0" max="4294967295" step="1" value="42"><button id="apply" disabled>Apply & reset</button></div><p id="settings-note" class="small" role="status">Controls apply with “Apply & reset”.</p>
+        <div class="comparison"><p class="eyebrow">03 / EXPERIMENT</p><h3>One ocean. Two beliefs.</h3><p>Keep every fix identical. Give a second filter a different R.</p><label for="compare-r">Alternative sensor σ (m)</label><input id="compare-r" type="number" min="0.2" max="8" step="0.1" value="2.4"><button id="compare" disabled>Compare the full mission ↗</button><div id="comparison-output" hidden></div></div>
+      </aside>
+    </div>
+    <section class="notebook" id="notebook" aria-labelledby="notebook-title"><div class="notebook-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / UNDERSTAND</p><h2 id="notebook-title">A little trust. A little correction.</h2></div><p>You don’t need matrices to begin.<br>Open them when you’re ready.</p></div>
+      <div class="lesson-grid"><article><span class="lesson-number">01</span><h3>Make a prediction.</h3><p>“I was here, moving this fast.” The model uses the last depth, velocity, and commanded acceleration to guess the next depth. Its uncertainty grows as unknown motion accumulates.</p></article><article><span class="lesson-number">02</span><h3>Listen to a fix.</h3><p>A processed localization fix gives a noisy depth. The <strong>innovation</strong> is the gap between this fix and the prediction. No fix? Keep the prediction and its growing uncertainty.</p></article><article><span class="lesson-number">03</span><h3>Decide how much to trust.</h3><p>The Kalman gain weights that gap. A larger R means less trust in the sensor. A larger Q means less trust in motion. Neither setting changes what actually happened.</p></article></div>
+      <details class="worked" open><summary>A correction, with your live numbers <span>+</span></summary><div class="worked-content"><p id="worked-intro">Take one step to inspect a real correction. Each step represents 0.5 seconds.</p><div class="equation-steps"><div><span>PREDICTED DEPTH</span><strong id="worked-prior">4.00 m</strong></div><div><span>+ GAIN × INNOVATION</span><strong id="worked-adjustment">Waiting for a fix</strong></div><div><span>= CORRECTED DEPTH</span><strong id="worked-result">4.00 m</strong></div></div><p id="worked-velocity" class="small">The filter also estimates velocity in m/s.</p></div></details>
+      <details><summary>Lift the cover: the model & matrices <span>+</span></summary><div class="model-copy"><p>State x = [depth (m), velocity (m/s)]. Down is positive. Known command u is acceleration (m/s²); h = 0.5 s. Starting belief: x = [4, 0.05], P = diag(1, 0.25). The simulation starts at the same known launch state; later truth is never supplied to the filter.</p><div class="formula">F = [[1, h], [0, 1]] &nbsp; G = [h²/2, h]ᵀ &nbsp; H = [1, 0]<br>x⁻ = Fx + Gu &nbsp; P⁻ = FPFᵀ + Q<br>Q = σₐ² GGᵀ &nbsp; R = σᵣ²<br>K = P⁻Hᵀ / (HP⁻Hᵀ + R)<br>x⁺ = x⁻ + K(z − Hx⁻)<br>P⁺ = (I − KH)P⁻(I − KH)ᵀ + KRKᵀ</div><p>Q models independent, constant acceleration disturbances in each interval. Its depth variance has units m², velocity variance (m/s)², and cross covariance m²/s. The last equation is the Joseph covariance update. In dropout, only prediction runs.</p><p>Slider values are <strong>standard deviations σ</strong>, not variances. Squaring the sensor slider gives R. Squaring the motion slider and multiplying by GGᵀ gives Q.</p><p>The mint band is <strong>estimate ±2√P₍depth,depth₎</strong>, a marginal depth interval with about 95% modeled probability under matched Gaussian assumptions. It is not measured error. Current and bias deliberately violate the model; a narrow band can still miss the truth.</p></div></details>
+      <div class="learner"><div><p class="eyebrow">TRY THIS IN YOUR NOTEBOOK</p><h3>Can confidence be misplaced?</h3><p>Run “A convincing lie” with seed 42. At the end, compare the actual error with the ±2σ band. Predict what a larger R will do before running the comparison.</p></div><details><summary>Reveal the observation <span>+</span></summary><p>A biased fix can pull the estimate away from reality while covariance stays small. Increasing R may slow that pull, but cannot identify or remove a persistent bias. A bias state or a second independent sensor would be a better model.</p></details></div>
+    </section>
+    <footer class="footer"><div><b>abyss /</b> A small lab for big questions.<p>RoboSub-inspired navigation. An educational simulation, not an official course or competition scoring system.</p></div><details><summary>Sources & simulation limits <span>+</span></summary><p>One depth axis, open-loop motion, Gaussian noise, instantaneous fixes, no collisions. Gate and bin markers are mission landmarks, not scored tasks. Processed localization fixes are simulated depth measurements, not raw sonar bearings, ranges, or underwater GPS. No DVL is simulated. Current adds unmodeled +0.012 m/s² from 18–32 s; bias adds +2.5 m to fixes from 20 s.</p><p>Read <a href="https://www.cs.unc.edu/~welch/media/pdf/kalman_intro.pdf">Welch & Bell’s Kalman introduction</a>, <a href="https://www.bzarg.com/p/how-a-kalman-filter-works-in-pictures/">Bzarg’s illustrated explanation</a>, and <a href="https://robonation.gitbook.io/robosub-resources/section-3-autonomy-challenge/3.2-task-descriptions">RoboNation’s autonomy tasks</a>. Accessibility informed by <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/">WCAG 2.2</a>.</p></details></footer>
+    <p id="announcement" class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
+  </main>
+</body>
+</html>
