+# Abyss / clarity delivery
+
+Complete standalone activity: **[kalman/index.html](kalman/index.html)**. Secret now has a fourth, accessible Abyss card and a four-project footer. No build, packages, backend, CDN, publishing, or commits are required or performed. All changes are inside this working copy. Rival implementations and reports were not inspected.
+
+## Setup and preview
+
+From this checkout, with Node installed:
+
+```powershell
+node tests/kalman-preview.cjs
+```
+
+Open **http://localhost:8311/kalman/**, or **http://localhost:8311/secret/** to use the fourth card. Port 8311 is the assigned clarity preview. The server binds to 127.0.0.1 and serves this checkout only. Stop it with Ctrl+C. The activity also works from a static server or by opening its HTML directly; it does not fetch data or require the Worker. Existing private upload APIs still require their existing Worker setup.
+
+## What is implemented
+
+- A 60-second depth mission, 120 fixed 0.5-second steps, initially paused. Native Start/Pause, Step, Reset, and endpoint Replay controls. Playback reveals about 3.3 mission seconds per wall second, identified beside progress. Switching away from the browser tab pauses playback.
+- Quiet water, localization dropout from 20–38 s, unmodeled current acceleration from 18–32 s, and persistent +2.5 m sensor bias from 20 s.
+- Independent controls for actual sensor standard deviation, assumed measurement standard deviation, and assumed acceleration disturbance standard deviation. Labels explain how these become R and Q. Seed input and explicit Apply & reset make the applied run reproducible. Scenario selection applies the selected mission immediately.
+- A custom responsive underwater SVG scene with a truth sub, solid truth trace, crossed orange fixes, circled mint estimate, modeled ±2σ depth band, and dotted dead reckoning. Route landmarks evoke gate/slalom/bin navigation; time is the horizontal axis, not horizontal position.
+- Current numerical truth/fix/estimate/velocity/error/interval text, raw/filter/dead-reckoning RMSE, fix counts, and finite summaries with actual error versus modeled confidence and interval coverage.
+- Same-data full-mission comparison with a second R, including identical raw RMSE, both filter RMSEs, and an optional gold dashed estimate revealed alongside the applied run. Results explicitly refer to a full 60-second replay, even when the live mission is partway through.
+- A field notebook that progresses from plain-language prediction and correction to live worked numbers, optional matrices and units, sensor/model limitations, and a bias challenge with a revealable explanation.
+- Semantic headings and labels, focus outlines, native keyboard controls, 44 px controls, shape distinctions, numerical plot equivalents, event-only announcements, reduced-motion CSS, and an actual no-JS explanation with simulation buttons disabled.
+
+## Numerical model and rationale
+
+The filter tracks depth and velocity. F = [[1,h],[0,1]], G = [h²/2,h]ᵀ, H = [1,0]. Known commanded acceleration enters prediction. Independent, constant acceleration disturbances in each interval give **Q = σₐ² GGᵀ**; **R = σᵣ²**. Correction uses Joseph covariance form. Missing fixes skip correction completely.
+
+`filter.js` separates data generation, prediction/correction, replay, and metrics. The generator receives the seed, actual noise, and scenario; assumed Q and R never participate. The filter sees only the command and fixes. Ground truth is used for visualization and evaluation. Both the simulated launch and initial estimate use the stated known state [4 m, 0.05 m/s]; the initial covariance is diag(1, 0.25).
+
+The editorial paper-and-ocean palette creates a guided notebook rather than a dense instrument wall. Color is supplemented with crosses, circles, and dash patterns. Math is available through native disclosures; the worked example comes directly from the simulation. This design rationale is a hypothesis, not user-study evidence.
+
+## Actual verification
+
+Final numerical and regression command:
+
+```powershell
+node --test tests/*.test.cjs
+```
+
+**28 tests passed, 0 failed.** Eight Kalman tests cover:
+
+1. Exact h=1, u=0, Q=0, R=1, x=[0,0], P=I, z=3 fixture: x=[2,1], K=[2/3,1/3], P=[[2/3,1/3],[1/3,2/3]].
+2. Known acceleration and discrete acceleration covariance.
+3. Every missing-fix step copies its prediction; uncertainty grows and contracts at recovery.
+4. Deterministic replay, different seeds, and tuning-independent truth/fixes for all scenarios.
+5. Poisoning every ground-truth value leaves all filter states and covariances unchanged.
+6. Bias and current scenario isolation.
+7. **30,000 updates**, including prolonged dropouts and extreme Q/R combinations, with finite states and finite, symmetric, positive semidefinite covariance.
+8. Finite mission endpoints and meaningful seed-42 RMSE/coverage.
+
+The other 20 tests cover the original navigation, native/modified click and keyboard behavior, Secret assets/cards/footer, Worker routes including all new Kalman assets, and private-upload functionality/session isolation. Worker and other activity implementations were not changed.
+
+Seed 42, actual sensor σ=1.2 m, assumed sensor σ=1.2 m, assumed acceleration σ=0.08 m/s²:
+
+| Mission | Raw fix RMSE (m) | Filter RMSE (m) | Dead reckoning RMSE (m) | Truth in ±2σ |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| Quiet water | 1.2253 | 0.4532 | 8.2378 | 98.3% |
+| Dropout | 1.2085 | 0.8807 | 8.2378 | 98.3% |
+| Current | 1.2253 | 0.4577 | 10.9005 | 98.3% |
+| Bias | 2.4179 | 2.1062 | 8.2378 | 33.3% |
+
+Raw RMSE uses available fixes; the other RMSEs use every elapsed step. These are one-seed measurements, not general performance guarantees.
+
+Syntax checked with `node --check` on `kalman/app.js`, `kalman/filter.js`, `tests/kalman-preview.cjs`, and `tests/kalman.test.cjs`. `git diff --check` passed. New files were checked separately with `git diff --no-index --check -- NUL <file>`; a trailing blank CSS line found there was removed and rechecked.
+
+**Actual Edge browser verification**, using the Browser skill:
+
+- Inspected **1440×900**, **390×844**, and **320×740**. Final measured document widths: 1425, 375, and 305 px respectively, with the browser scrollbar accounting for the difference. No horizontal overflow. Button heights were 44 px at each size; scenario rows and disclosures met or exceeded 44 px.
+- Clicked the fourth Secret card and observed the Abyss activity. Verified native `_blank`/noopener markup and four-card footer through regression tests and browser DOM inspection. The automation did not independently establish a newly created native browser window count.
+- Verified initially paused state, Enter stepping, live worked correction, start/pause, reset/replay, finite nominal/dropout/bias endpoints, disabled endpoint step button, and progress value 120/120. Current’s unmodeled motion event was observed at 23 s; its full-run endpoint and metrics are additionally covered by the numerical tests.
+- Verified exact first-step UI replay. Changed assumed R to 16 m² and assumed acceleration σ to 0.09 m/s² with keyboard keys: the fix stayed **3.69 m** while the assumptions changed. Changed actual sensor σ to 3 m: that fix became **2.64 m**. Keyboard focus outline observed on Step.
+- Paused dropout at **33.5 s**: no fix, prediction-only worked example, ±2σ **5.54 m**, actual error **1.81 m**. Final dropout summary had 84 fixes and a **0.61 m** final error. Bias finished with **1.90 m** actual error against **±0.98 m** modeled confidence.
+- Compared nominal R=1.44 versus R=5.76: full-run filter RMSE **0.45 versus 0.48 m**, both raw RMSE **1.23 m**. Dropout comparison gave **0.88 versus 1.28 m**, both raw RMSE **1.21 m**, with the same 84 fixes.
+- Opened model disclosure with Enter. Verified the actual activity’s `<noscript>` explanation and disabled buttons inside `tests/kalman-no-js-preview.html`, which uses a script-disabled sandbox. Normal activity browser warning/error logs were empty during final checks.
+
+Evidence is in **[work/verification](work/verification/)**. Primary visual evidence: [desktop](work/verification/kalman-desktop.png), [390 px phone](work/verification/kalman-phone.png), [full phone page](work/verification/kalman-phone-full.png), [320 px](work/verification/kalman-320.png), and [dropout](work/verification/kalman-dropout-320.png). JSON audits record viewport widths, control dimensions, tuning checks, nominal/bias summaries, and the dropout state. Early `*-initial` screenshots are intermediate work; final named screenshots and audits are the review artifacts.
+
+## Limits and unsupported checks
+
+This is a linear, one-axis, open-loop teaching model: no collision/contact physics, underwater GPS, raw sonar range/bearing inversion, DVL, closed-loop navigation, or official competition scoring. Fixes represent simulated processed localization depth. Gaussian uncertainty is conditional on the model; current and bias deliberately violate it. A larger R does not remove bias. No claim is made that filtering or any one tuning always improves RMSE.
+
+Real assistive-technology sessions, physical touch devices, other browser engines, OS reduced-motion emulation, and a formal WCAG audit were **not performed**. The motion preference is honored in CSS, and mission playback always requires explicit input. Performance benchmarking and production Cloudflare/R2 deployment were not performed. Browser screenshot capture sometimes lagged a preceding layout or playback change; final paused captures were saved after independent DOM audits. One excessive batch of browser steps timed out; it was retried through bounded playback and inspected states, and is not counted as a pass.
+
+## Review loop
+
+Cycle 1: **8/10**. Numerical/regression gates passed; playback placement and stale label after stepping needed fixes.
+
+Cycle 2: **9/10**. Controls moved above the scene, step label corrected, exact fractional depth ticks retained, playback speed labeled, CSS formatted, and the required checks completed. All mandatory implementation criteria are verified; no required revisions remain. Two of the maximum three cycles were used. Progress record: [work/goal-loop-state.md](work/goal-loop-state.md).
